{"outcome":"DIRECT_HIGH_QUALITY","best_model_id":"PGS001312","confidence":"High","rationale":"Endpoint fidelity: PGS001312 is a direct match to the target trait (trait_efo=psoriasis; phenotyping_reported=Psoriasis). Competing candidates include psoriatic arthritis/arthropathy (PGS000342, PGS001287) or severity-focused endpoints (e.g., PGS004315/4316; PGS005307+), which are not as clean a match for generic psoriasis risk per the endpoint-fidelity guidance (prs_model_evaluator skill section: trait_labels).

Performance evidence (PRS-comparable): PGS001312 reports explicit PRS-only metrics in Europeans (PGS AUROC no covariates 0.6916; PGS R2 no covariates 0.0523) with a large validation sample (n=67,425) and only basic covariates in the full model (age/sex/PCs/array). Many other psoriasis candidates here either lack PRS-only AUC/R2 entirely (e.g., partial-r only for PGS001871/PGS002083; incremental R2 only for the Nat Genet set; effect-size-only for several newer severity scores) or use non-generic endpoints (time-to-event for PGS001313). This aligns with the metric-interpretation guidance that PRS-only R2/AUC are the most reliable cross-model signals (prs_model_evaluator skill section: performance_metrics).

Heritability sanity check: Local EUR h2 records for psoriasis show observed-scale h2 around ~0.0013–0.0023 for ICD10/self-reported psoriasis, with liability-scale h2 around ~0.08–0.16 (and up to ~0.127 for self-reported psoriasis). PGS001312’s PRS-only R2=0.052 is plausible relative to these liability-scale h2 values (i.e., not exceeding a reasonable heritability ceiling), supporting that the reported PRS-only metric is not obviously inconsistent (tool: get_heritability_records('psoriasis'))."}
